A||||10||sjp777||@home and AT &T can bite me||||8||
Z||000000||sjp777||05-29-2001||11:02 PM||||Got home from work today and found a letter from AT&T broadband telling me that my monthly bill for cable internet was going up to $45.95<P>They got some nerve. Their service has pretty much sucked for the better part of the last year, and their customer service is the worst I have ever encountered.<P>They did some upgrades about 2 months ago so lately there haven't been any problems. I guess they figure now would be a good time to jack up the price.<P>I immediatly called and cancelled my service. I made sure they knew why. Then I called Qwest and got DSL for $37.95, plus a free first month and a free modem that I can keep, unlike the AT&T leased modem.<P>I'm sure the DSL price will follow the cable raping soon, but if enough people start cancelling in response to the rate increases, maybe they'll think twice.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg">    <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||8
Z||000001||Oreif||05-29-2001||11:52 PM||||There are many Internet Providers raising their rates. AOL, MSN, Earthlink, AT&T, Sprint, ETC. There was something in the news a few weeks ago about Everyone's rates will be going up. Most are raising them by $6.00.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||05-30-2001||02:47 AM||||Cable is already higher than that here in Nashville. Mine is only $40 per month, but I save about $10 per month because my girlfriend works at Vanderbilt and we get a discount because of it...<P>Someone down in GA told me that there is no true satellite access available that requires no modem for upstream. Sounds pretty cool and pretty fast... as long as the weather is nice. Worth watching though.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tweek||05-30-2001||12:29 PM||||My cable provider offers a package for 29.99, though its not exactly what I would call screamin.. I much prefer cable over dsl, mainly for reliability.||||reg||1
Z||000004||kslish||05-30-2001||12:43 PM||||I have AT&T @home and I got that rate increase letter also.  I was only paying $29.95/month since I bought my modem for $99 after rebate at Circuit City (it's already paid for itself).  Looks like I'm going to get upped to $35.95/month.  <P>Unfortunately, they'll have to up it a lot more before I consider getting rid of it...I'm addicted to the speed and the freedom from not tying up a phone line.  That and DSL is not really built up in my area due to Verizon dragging their feet and the companies that do offer it charge $49.95/month.  I really wish DSL would be more competitive though so prices would stay constant.<P>Ken S.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Taijiguy||05-30-2001||02:30 PM||||I just signed up for DSL through Ameritech. I was paying almost 85 bucks a month for 56K ISDN! Between the charges for the phone line, and the ISP that's what it added up to. I looked around, and the best price I found for unlimted DSL was around 49 bucks a month. Ameritech has a package that give full featured phone service (all the goodies) plus DSL service for like, 90 a month. Free adaptor, and no charge for self install. Figured I'd give that a try.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Songman||05-30-2001||04:25 PM||||I still pay the higher charge because I opted not to buy my modem. I would rather let them just bring me another one if it messes up. They have already had to do that once.<P>The CyberSURFR like I have is about $400! It will take a while at $10 per month savings to pay for it..<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||05-30-2001||05:21 PM||||Ill stick with corecom till something new comes along. its a little slow, not to many boots. never busy sig, only $10 @ month unlimited.||||reg||1
Z||000008||kslish||05-30-2001||10:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>I still pay the higher charge because I opted not to buy my modem. I would rather let them just bring me another one if it messes up. They have already had to do that once.<P>The CyberSURFR like I have is about $400! It will take a while at $10 per month savings to pay for it..<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The cable modems that AT&T initally used were notoriously unreliable.  Cable modems are pretty much all the same as long as they follow the CableLabs standards.  The Toshiba PCX1100 I bought is CableLabs certified and is endorsed by AT&T (actually AT&T has switched to USRobotics cable modems in my area if you rent from them and they sell them for $299, about a $100 markup).  The Toshiba modem is the cheapest I found ($149-$199 regular priced but I bought it when they were offering a mail in rebate, so final price was $99).  And it comes with a 5 year warranty so I'm not concerned if it fails (but its been rock solid for the past year).  <P>Ken S.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Taijiguy||05-30-2001||11:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>Ill stick with corecom till something new comes along. its a little slow, not to many boots. never busy sig, only $10 @ month unlimited.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I have the exact opposite experience with them! I get booted 3 times a day! That's what prompted me to look into DSL.<BR>||||reg||1
